# KnowledgeOS - APIs

---

# 1. Purpose

The API layer serves as the communication bridge between the React frontend and the FastAPI backend.

It exposes a set of secure REST endpoints that allow authenticated users to interact with every feature of KnowledgeOS, including:

- Authentication
- Document Management
- Folder Management
- AI Conversations
- Knowledge Retrieval
- Personalized Insights
- User Preferences

The API layer is responsible for:

- Validating incoming requests
- Authenticating users
- Authorizing resource access
- Coordinating AI pipelines
- Managing database operations
- Returning standardized responses

The API design follows REST principles while remaining modular enough to support future migration to GraphQL or gRPC if required.

---

# 2. API Design Principles

KnowledgeOS APIs are designed according to modern backend engineering best practices.

## RESTful Resource Design

Every endpoint represents a logical resource rather than an action.

Example:

```text
/users

/documents

/folders

/chat

/insights
```

instead of

```text
/getDocuments

/createFolder

/deleteChat
```

---

## Stateless Communication

Every request contains all information necessary for processing.

The backend never relies on previous HTTP requests to maintain state.

Conversation state is persisted inside PostgreSQL rather than server memory.

---

## JWT-Based Authentication

Protected endpoints require a valid Supabase JWT access token.

Authentication is verified before any business logic executes.

Unauthenticated requests are rejected immediately.

---

## User Isolation

Every authenticated request is automatically scoped using the authenticated user's `profile_id`.

No endpoint allows direct access to another user's data.

Authorization checks occur before database queries.

---

## Consistent URL Structure

KnowledgeOS follows consistent endpoint naming.

Example:

```text
/api/v1/documents

/api/v1/chat

/api/v1/insights
```

This simplifies maintenance and future versioning.

---

## Standard HTTP Methods

| Method | Purpose |
|---------|----------|
| GET | Retrieve resources |
| POST | Create resources |
| PUT | Replace resources |
| PATCH | Partial updates |
| DELETE | Delete resources |

---

## Standard HTTP Status Codes

| Status | Meaning |
|---------|----------|
| 200 | Success |
| 201 | Resource Created |
| 204 | No Content |
| 400 | Bad Request |
| 401 | Unauthorized |
| 403 | Forbidden |
| 404 | Resource Not Found |
| 409 | Conflict |
| 422 | Validation Error |
| 429 | Too Many Requests |
| 500 | Internal Server Error |

---

## Standard JSON Responses

Every endpoint returns JSON.

Successful responses use a consistent format.

Errors also follow a standardized schema.

---

## API Documentation

All APIs are documented using OpenAPI.

FastAPI automatically generates:

- Swagger UI
- ReDoc Documentation
- OpenAPI Specification

This provides interactive testing during development.

