# 6. Document APIs

The Document APIs manage document upload, organization, retrieval, deletion, restoration, and viewing.

Documents represent the primary knowledge source within KnowledgeOS.

Supported document formats include:

- PDF
- DOCX
- PPTX
- Markdown
- TXT
- HTML

Quick Notes are automatically converted into TXT documents and stored using the same pipeline.

---

## Upload Document

```http
POST /api/v1/documents/upload
```

Purpose

Uploads one or more documents.

Supports

- Single upload
- Multiple upload
- Drag and Drop
- Progress tracking

Validation

- Supported file type
- Maximum file size
- Virus scanning (future)
- Duplicate detection (future)

Response

```http
202 Accepted
```

The upload pipeline continues asynchronously.

---

## Get Documents

```http
GET /api/v1/documents
```

Returns

- Uploaded documents
- Folder information
- Processing status
- File size
- Upload date

Supports

- Pagination
- Sorting
- Search
- Filters

---

## Get Document Details

```http
GET /api/v1/documents/{document_id}
```

Returns

- Metadata
- Processing status
- Version
- File information
- AI statistics

---

## Open Document

```http
GET /api/v1/documents/{document_id}/view
```

Purpose

Streams the document directly inside the browser.

The document is **displayed**, not downloaded.

This powers the built-in document viewer.

---

## Download Document

```http
GET /api/v1/documents/{document_id}/download
```

Downloads the original uploaded file.

---

## Move Document

```http
PATCH /api/v1/documents/{document_id}/move
```

Request

```json
{
    "folder_id": "..."
}
```

Moves a document into another folder.

---

## Rename Document

```http
PATCH /api/v1/documents/{document_id}
```

Allows users to rename uploaded documents without modifying the original file.

---

## Soft Delete Document

```http
DELETE /api/v1/documents/{document_id}
```

Purpose

Moves a document into **Recently Deleted**.

Backend Operations

- Set `is_deleted = true`
- Set `deleted_at`
- Hide document from library
- Exclude from RAG retrieval
- Exclude from Insights generation

The ChromaDB metadata filter immediately prevents deleted documents from being retrieved by the AI.

---

## Restore Document

```http
POST /api/v1/documents/{document_id}/restore
```

Restores a soft-deleted document.

The document immediately becomes available for:

- Search
- Retrieval
- AI Chat
- Insights

---

## Permanently Delete Document

```http
DELETE /api/v1/documents/{document_id}/permanent
```

Backend Workflow

```text
Delete Request

↓

Delete ChromaDB Embeddings

↓

Delete Document Chunks

↓

Delete PostgreSQL Metadata

↓

Delete Original File

↓

Return Success
```

This operation is irreversible.

---

## Favorite Document

```http
PATCH /api/v1/documents/{document_id}/favorite
```

Marks or unmarks a document as a favorite.

---

## Search Documents

```http
GET /api/v1/documents/search
```

Supports

- Filename
- Folder
- Tags (future)
- Document type
- Upload date

---

# 7. Upload Pipeline APIs

Uploading a document starts an asynchronous AI processing pipeline.

---

## Upload Processing Flow

```text
Upload

↓

Store Original File

↓

Extract Text

↓

Chunk Generation

↓

Metadata Extraction

↓

Embedding Generation

↓

ChromaDB Storage

↓

Processing Complete
```

---

## Get Processing Status

```http
GET /api/v1/documents/{document_id}/status
```

Returns

```json
{
    "status": "processing",
    "progress": 65
}
```

Processing States

- Uploaded
- Parsing
- Chunking
- Embedding
- Completed
- Failed

---

## Retry Processing

```http
POST /api/v1/documents/{document_id}/retry
```

Retries failed ingestion.

Only available when

```text
processing_status = failed
```

---

## Cancel Processing

```http
POST /api/v1/documents/{document_id}/cancel
```

Cancels a running ingestion job.

Partially generated chunks and embeddings are automatically cleaned up to maintain consistency between PostgreSQL and ChromaDB.

---

## Processing WebSocket (Future)

```text
/ws/upload-progress
```

Provides real-time upload and ingestion progress updates without polling, enabling a smoother user experience for large document uploads.

